<p>To begin, we create a new <code>AuthController</code> class that will handle user authentication. This includes two primary actions: user registration and user login. By using this controller, users will be able to create accounts and log in to receive a JWT, which they can use to access protected endpoints.</p>
<p>Here&#x27;s how it works:</p>
<ul>
<li>The <code>AuthController</code> uses <code>UserManager</code> for user operations, <code>SignInManager</code> for handling sign-ins, and <code>IConfiguration</code> for accessing JWT settings.</li>
<li>The <code>Register</code> method creates a new user with the provided details. Once created, the user is assigned the &quot;User&quot; role. If registration succeeds, an <code>Ok</code> response is returned; otherwise, a <code>BadRequest</code> with errors is sent.</li>
<li>The <code>Login</code> method verifies if the email exists and checks the password. On success, a JWT token is generated and returned for authenticated access.</li>
<li>The <code>GenerateJwtToken</code> method creates a token with the user&#x27;s ID and email as claims. It signs the token using the secret key from <code>appsettings.json</code> and sets it to expire in 3 hours.</li>
</ul>
